1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,655
Tax depends on what you sell and where the buyer is.

2
00:00:04,655 --> 00:00:10,642
This video shows why the Taxation module exists, how categories, jurisdictions, rules and

3
00:00:10,642 --> 00:00:15,810
tables fit together, and how to use every screen, up to the tax at checkout.

4
00:00:20,410 --> 00:00:25,229
Selling online means charging tax, and the right tax depends on what you

5
00:00:25,229 --> 00:00:27,330
sell and where the buyer is.

6
00:00:27,330 --> 00:00:31,160
A flat percentage on everything is almost never correct.

7
00:00:31,910 --> 00:00:36,853
Done by hand, tax is a spreadsheet of rates that changes without warning,

8
00:00:36,853 --> 00:00:40,170
and every mistake lands on your own tax return.

9
00:00:40,920 --> 00:00:44,299
The Taxation module keeps the rules in one place:

10
00:00:44,299 --> 00:00:49,460
which taxes exist, where they apply, to which kinds of products, at what rate.

11
00:00:50,210 --> 00:00:53,948
At checkout the right tax is worked out for every order and shown

12
00:00:53,948 --> 00:00:57,580
to the buyer, and the order keeps a record of what was charged.

13
00:01:01,780 --> 00:01:06,424
Tax categories group your products, such as clothing or books.

14
00:01:06,424 --> 00:01:10,180
Tax types name the tax, such as sales tax or VAT.

15
00:01:10,930 --> 00:01:14,638
Jurisdictions are the places that charge tax:

16
00:01:14,638 --> 00:01:17,910
a country, a state, a county or a city.

17
00:01:18,660 --> 00:01:24,571
Rules say which tax applies to which category in which jurisdiction, and at what rate.

18
00:01:24,571 --> 00:01:28,040
Tax tables hold rates that depend on the amount.

19
00:01:28,790 --> 00:01:34,268
Settings, Commerce, Tax origin says where you sell from, and the Taxation part

20
00:01:34,268 --> 00:01:38,050
on a content type puts its products into the system.

21
00:01:42,247 --> 00:01:45,066
Open Commerce, Taxation, Categories.

22
00:01:45,066 --> 00:01:49,900
A category groups products that are taxed alike, such as clothing.

23
00:01:49,900 --> 00:01:51,847
Click Add Tax Category.

24
00:01:52,298 --> 00:01:54,309
Enter a Name and a Code.

25
00:01:54,309 --> 00:02:00,209
Parent code nests a category inside another, and the Description is for your team.

26
00:02:00,209 --> 00:02:01,348
Click Save.

27
00:02:01,799 --> 00:02:09,684
Commerce, Taxation, Types lists the kinds of tax, such as SalesTax, VAT, GST and TourismTax.

28
00:02:09,684 --> 00:02:12,339
Add Tax Type adds your own.

29
00:02:16,534 --> 00:02:22,213
Open Commerce, Taxation, Jurisdictions and click Add Tax Jurisdiction.

30
00:02:22,213 --> 00:02:25,874
A jurisdiction is a place that charges tax.

31
00:02:26,325 --> 00:02:32,154
Enter the Name and a Code, then choose its Level, such as State, and the Country.

32
00:02:32,154 --> 00:02:36,575
Region, County, City and Postal code narrow it down further.

33
00:02:37,029 --> 00:02:42,539
A Parent jurisdiction nests a place inside another, and Effective from and Effective

34
00:02:42,539 --> 00:02:44,438
to limit when it applies.

35
00:02:44,438 --> 00:02:45,479
Click Save.

36
00:02:49,723 --> 00:02:54,188
Open Commerce, Taxation, Rules and click Add Tax Rule.

37
00:02:54,188 --> 00:03:01,927
Rules come in several kinds, such as Percentage, Fixed amount, Per unit, Per weight and Threshold.

38
00:03:01,927 --> 00:03:03,713
Choose Percentage.

39
00:03:04,164 --> 00:03:08,123
Give the rule a Name, choose the Tax type, and a Display name,

40
00:03:08,123 --> 00:03:10,918
which is what the buyer sees on the order.

41
00:03:10,918 --> 00:03:14,993
The Jurisdiction can limit the rule to one place, or stay on Any

42
00:03:14,993 --> 00:03:18,544
jurisdiction, and the Category says what it applies to.

43
00:03:18,995 --> 00:03:22,691
Customer type limits it to consumers or to businesses.

44
00:03:22,691 --> 00:03:27,494
Minimum amount and Maximum amount limit it by price, and Tax is included

45
00:03:27,494 --> 00:03:32,175
in the item price takes the tax out of prices that already contain it.

46
00:03:32,629 --> 00:03:38,371
Tax is compound charges it on top of other taxes, Reverse charge leaves

47
00:03:38,371 --> 00:03:44,487
the tax to the customer, and Applies to shipping charges taxes shipping too.

48
00:03:44,487 --> 00:03:50,529
Enter the Rate as a fraction, so 0.0875 means 8.75 percent, and click Save.

49
00:03:54,829 --> 00:03:57,380
Open Settings, Commerce, Tax origin.

50
00:03:57,380 --> 00:04:01,753
Enter the Country and the State or province you sell from, and the

51
00:04:01,753 --> 00:04:03,879
address if tax depends on it.

52
00:04:08,070 --> 00:04:10,799
Products need the Taxation part.

53
00:04:10,799 --> 00:04:17,190
Open Content, Content Definition, Content Types, edit Product, and click Add Parts.

54
00:04:17,640 --> 00:04:24,000
Tick Taxation, which classifies a product for taxation without storing a rate, and add it.

55
00:04:24,451 --> 00:04:27,140
Click Edit next to the Taxation part.

56
00:04:27,140 --> 00:04:31,141
Default tax category is the category new items start with.

57
00:04:31,141 --> 00:04:33,141
Choose Clothing, and save.

58
00:04:33,592 --> 00:04:34,956
Open a product.

59
00:04:34,956 --> 00:04:37,553
Under Taxation, Taxable is ticked.

60
00:04:37,553 --> 00:04:43,982
Choose Clothing as the Tax category, so the rules for that category apply, and click Publish.

61
00:04:48,159 --> 00:04:52,447
At checkout, the order summary now shows a Subtotal, and a line for

62
00:04:52,447 --> 00:04:57,089
each tax, such as Sales tax and its rate, with what it adds to the total.

63
00:04:57,546 --> 00:05:00,952
Due now is what the buyer pays, tax included.

64
00:05:00,952 --> 00:05:07,096
The order keeps every tax it was charged, so reports and invoices show the same lines.

65
00:05:11,396 --> 00:05:16,857
Commerce, Taxation, Tables holds a list of amount ranges, each with its own

66
00:05:16,857 --> 00:05:21,576
rate, for the Tax table lookup, Progressive and Threshold rules.

67
00:05:22,036 --> 00:05:27,925
Settings, Commerce, TaxJar works out United States sales tax by state, county and

68
00:05:27,925 --> 00:05:32,256
city, from your TaxJar account, instead of your own rules.

69
00:05:32,713 --> 00:05:37,565
The EU VAT standard rates recipe adds a VAT rule for every member

70
00:05:37,565 --> 00:05:42,621
state, and an Import duty rule charges duty on orders above a value.

71
00:05:42,621 --> 00:05:47,883
The VAT one-stop shop report adds up VAT charged to other EU countries.

72
00:05:52,083 --> 00:05:53,158
A US shop:

73
00:05:53,158 --> 00:05:57,927
a sales tax rule for your state, and tax by category, so clothing

74
00:05:57,927 --> 00:06:00,413
and food are taxed differently.

75
00:06:01,163 --> 00:06:02,785
A shop in the EU:

76
00:06:02,785 --> 00:06:08,143
VAT rules for every country you sell to, with prices that include VAT.

77
00:06:08,893 --> 00:06:10,220
Selling abroad:

78
00:06:10,220 --> 00:06:14,834
an import duty rule that charges duty on large orders, so the buyer

79
00:06:14,834 --> 00:06:16,793
pays nothing on delivery.

80
00:06:17,543 --> 00:06:18,977
Business customers:

81
00:06:18,977 --> 00:06:24,023
a rule limited to Business customers, with reverse charge where the law allows it.

82
00:06:26,023 --> 00:06:30,435
Set the tax up once, by category and by place, and every order

83
00:06:30,435 --> 00:06:32,446
is charged the right tax.

84
00:06:32,446 --> 00:06:34,133
Thanks for watching.

